/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (Bluetooth attacks pose unique risks because they are proximity-based, silent, and difficult for users to detect. Unlike network-based attacks that may trigger firewall alerts or antivirus warnings, Bluetooth exploitation occurs at the physical layer with minimal observable indicators. A compromised Bluetooth device can be exploited in public spaces such as offices, public transport, and cafes, without any visible indication to the victim.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
