264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (The proposed framework enhances user privacy and security through multiple mechanisms. By making device security status visible and enforceable, it reduces the window of vulnerability exploitation from months or years to days or weeks. The risk-based approach ensures that critical functionality \(such as audio output for emergency calls\) can be maintained even for high-risk devices, while sensitive capabilities are appropriately restricted.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (SECURITY BENEFITS)
/E (SECURITY BENEFITS)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (The framework aligns with ethical hacking and responsible disclosure principles by raising the difficulty of exploitation and reducing trivial attack paths. It empowers users with information and control over their security posture without requiring deep technical knowledge. Transparency in risk scoring helps users make informed decisions about device usage and replacement.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS)
/E (ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (User-visible risk indicators and functionality restrictions create economic incentives for vendors to maintain security support throughout reasonable product lifecycles. Devices that receive regular security updates and provide accurate security metadata will be rewarded with better user experience and reduced negative publicity.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (VENDOR INCENTIVES)
/E (VENDOR INCENTIVES)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
